      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: A2A handoffs can duplicate message-tool replies",
        "body": "Related: #39476\nRelated: #91161\nRelated: #93293\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users asking an agent to hand work to another session could receive duplicate visible output when the target session replied through `message(action=\"send\")` and the waited A2A path later treated transcript bookkeeping as a fresh assistant reply.\n\nThis PR was triggered by a real local WhatsApp/Main Merid duplicate-delivery report. The private message content is intentionally not included, but the observed shape was: one correct requester-visible reply, followed by a second visible message derived from the same A2A/source-reply flow.\n\nThis is a narrow companion to #39476. It does not replace #91161's reverse `sessions_send` tool guard, and it does not change compaction replay behavior covered by #93293.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix keeps waited A2A reply extraction on model-authored assistant replies instead of transcript artifacts. It excludes inter-session input rows, raw OpenClaw delivery mirrors, projected message-tool mirrors, and Gateway-injected assistant rows before they can feed ping-pong or announce delivery.\n\nIt also keeps same-session A2A source replies from re-running the announce decider when there is no valid announce target, and treats incomplete-turn fallback text as non-deliverable in the A2A announce path.\n\nNo production config, secrets, channel adapter contract, tool schema, delivery API, runtime permission, package metadata, or changelog file is changed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nA2A handoffs that reply visibly through the message tool no longer turn already-delivered source replies or forwarded `sessions_send` transcript rows into a second visible message. Normal model-authored assistant replies still use the existing waited reply, ping-pong, and announce behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent-head proof after rebasing onto `upstream/main` `d633a2df422`; pushed PR head `8221d42bf1`. Latest checked upstream still has the unfiltered waited A2A reply path, and the rebased branch merges cleanly.\n\nRedacted Gateway/channel proof using the repo QA suite:\n\n```text\nOPENCLAW_BUILD_ALL_NO_PNPM=1 \\\nOPENCLAW_RUN_NODE_SKIP_DTS_BUILD=1 \\\nOPENCLAW_TSDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=180000 \\\nOPENCLAW_HOME=\"$PWD/.artifacts/openclaw-home-pr97259-scope-narrow-rebase-20260707\" \\\nOPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=\"$PWD/.artifacts/openclaw-state-pr97259-scope-narrow-rebase-20260707\" \\\nOPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=\"$PWD/.artifacts/openclaw-state-pr97259-scope-narrow-rebase-20260707/openclaw.json\" \\\nnode scripts/run-node.mjs qa suite --provider-mode mock-openai --transport qa-channel \\\n  --scenario a2a-message-tool-mirror-dedupe \\\n  --output-dir .artifacts/qa-e2e/a2a-message-tool-mirror-dedupe-pr97259-scope-narrow-rebase-20260707\n\nPassed: 1\nFailed: 0\n```\n\nThe QA scenario runs a real Gateway child with `qa-channel` and `mock-openai`, then proves:\n\n```text\noutbound=group:qa-a2a-mirror-room:QA-A2A-MESSAGE-TOOL-MIRROR-OK\nsourceTool={\"sessionKey\":\"agent:qa:qa-channel:group:group:qa-a2a-mirror-room\",\"message\":\"qa group visible reply tool check. Use the visible room reply path. exact marker: `QA-A2A-MESSAGE-TOOL-MIRROR-OK`\",\"timeoutSeconds\":0}\ntargetTool={\"action\":\"send\",\"message\":\"QA-A2A-MESSAGE-TOOL-MIRROR-OK\"}\nduplicateWindowMs=8000\n```\n\nThat gives one source `sessions_send`, one target `message(action=\"send\")`, and exactly one requester-visible marker after the duplicate window.\n\nFocused regression tests:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/agents/run-wait.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/tools/sessions-send-tool.a2a.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/tools/sessions.test.ts \\\n  src/gateway/server.sessions-send.test.ts \\\n  extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-catalog.test.ts \\\n  extensions/qa-lab/src/providers/mock-openai/server.test.ts\n\nGateway shard:      2 files, 10 tests passed\nAgents shard:       3 files, 102 tests passed\nExtension QA shard: 2 files, 154 tests passed\n```\n\nTargeted local checks:\n\n```text\ngit diff --check upstream/main...HEAD\n# passed\n\n./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 <changed files>\n# passed\n\nnode scripts/run-oxlint.mjs <changed TypeScript files>\n# passed\n```\n\nNo live production WhatsApp message was sent for this proof. The behavior proof uses the repo's QA Gateway/channel harness with redacted deterministic markers.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Prepared with Codex, and I understand the code change.\n\n",
